{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A new wife.</b> Some say: a virgin. According to the view of the many, 'new' is set in contrast, for one could object: a divorced woman too, if she was not defiled. Therefore 'new.'" "<b>He shall be free for his house.</b> That the yoke of the kingdom not be upon him." "<b>נקי</b> like אי נקי." "For the one who says <b>לכל דבר</b> — it is superfluous, like והשלישי לאבשלום."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:36.076205993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}